{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And all these blessings shall come upon you and overtake you.</b> Regarding the matter of being supreme above all the nations of the earth, it says ״וּנְתָנְךָ ה׳״ — 'and HaShem will set you' — it suspends the matter upon the Holy One, blessed be He. But concerning the arrival of the rest of the blessings, it says ״וּבָאוּ״, meaning on their own; and who is it that pursues after them, that it says ״וְהִשִּׂיגֻךָ״ — 'and they shall overtake you'? The explanation is that everyone who pursues authority, it flees from him; and he who flees from authority, authority pursues after him (Tanhuma, Vayikra 3). And authority is the source of all blessings, for whatever a servant acquires, his master acquires. Therefore it says: ״וּנְתָנְךָ ה׳ עֶלְיוֹן״ etc., for this is authority, which is not fitting for you to seek or to strive after, yet in any case HaShem will give it to you. And from then onward, authority will pursue after you and overtake you; and along with authority, all these blessings will come on their own — for as they go in the train of authority that pursues after you, so all the blessings will pursue after you without your turning after them; and they shall overtake you along with authority, for through it you will acquire all the blessings of all the nations of the earth, for whatever a servant acquires, his master acquires."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:14:10.685375039Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}